+- [x] Thread `sessionStore` into `createMessageHandler` (optional parameter so existing 1-arg and 2-arg callers keep working) and wire it in `src/transport/createServer.ts`.
+- [x] Validate `list_sessions` frames in `src/transport/ws/validation.ts` (optional non-negative integer `limit`; optional `before` object with 1–128 char `sessionId` and finite-date `updatedAt` string or number; strip unknown fields like `userId`).
+- [x] Handle `list_sessions` in `src/transport/ws/messageHandler.ts` by reading `session.userId`, calling `await sessionStore?.listFor?.(session.userId, {limit, before})`, serialising `Date` fields to ISO strings, and on error logging via `log.error('ws', ...)` and sending `ErrorCodes.SERVER_ERROR`. Answered on the non-locked path beside `ping`, so a history request never queues behind a streaming turn.
+- [x] Document `list_sessions` and `session_list` in `specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md` (the conversation-list spec already carries the three transport statements, cited to the acceptance tests). Done as § 4.3 and § 5.9 — the two frames, their field tables, the authorisation rule (user id from the connection, never the frame; metadata, never content) and the INVALID_MESSAGE constraints, each cited to the tests that hold.
+
